<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kukdong shares available to foreigners.</title>
<headline>Kukdong shares available to foreigners.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities Supervisory Board said on Thursday 1.2 million shares of Kukdong City Gas Co, or 20 percent of the company's outstanding shares issued, would become available for foreign investment from Saturday.  </p>
<p>The stock market watchdog said in a statement foreigners had so far been barred from buying any Kukdong shares because a French firm held a 28 percent stake in the company.</p>
<p>The aggregate foreign ownership in most South Korean listed companies is currently limited at a maximum 20 percent.</p>
<p>Esys Montenay SA recently sold off its stake in Kukdong to LG-Caltex Oil Corp and LG Cable and Machinery Ltd, both affiliates of the LG Group.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
